---
description: Wrap UI components in a section named after the component
globs: src/components/**/*.jsx
alwaysApply: false
---

# UI component wrapper

When building a UI component, the outermost element must be a `<section>` whose class is the component name.

Keep existing visual/BEM classes on the same element when the root is already a styled tag. Do not wrap tiny helpers (icons, one-off inner cards) this way — only exported UI components.

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — root is a div, class does not match the component
export default function SpendingStats({ thisMonthSpent }) {
  return (
    <div className="stats">
      <p>{thisMonthSpent}</p>
    </div>
  )
}

// ✅ GOOD — root is section, first class is the component name
export default function SpendingStats({ thisMonthSpent }) {
  return (
    <section className="SpendingStats section">
      <p>{thisMonthSpent}</p>
    </section>
  )
}
```
